---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ExternalLink from "@/components/ExternalLink.astro";
import StateLink from "@/components/StateLink.astro";
import { ROUTES, ANCHORS } from "@/lib/routes";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About projectcert — mission, approach, and how to contribute."
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-8">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-ink">About</h1>

    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-muted">
      projectcert is an atlas of teacher certification requirements for
      instructing classified English Learner (EL) students across the
      fifty U.S. states and the District of Columbia.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Background</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">
      Under <em>Lau v. Nichols</em>, 414 U.S. 563 (1974), and
      subsequent federal civil-rights regulations, students classified
      as English Learners are entitled to meaningful access to the
      curriculum. Realization of that entitlement turns substantially
      on the preparation of the teacher of record. State education
      agencies (SEAs) set the credentialing requirements for teachers
      of ELs; those requirements vary considerably. This catalog
      documents the resulting variation.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Contents</h2>
    <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-6 text-ink-muted space-y-1">
      <li>An <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href={ROUTES.map}>interactive map</a> presenting six encoded variables.</li>
      <li>Cross-state reports on <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href={ROUTES.credentials.bilingual}>bilingual</a>, <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href={ROUTES.credentials.eld}>ELD</a>, and <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href={ROUTES.credentials.sei}>SEI</a> credentials.</li>
      <li>A <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href={ROUTES.compare}>side-by-side state comparison</a> tool.</li>
      <li>An individual record for each of the 51 jurisdictions (e.g., <StateLink usps="MA">Massachusetts</StateLink>).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Source paper</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">
      Leider, C. M., Colombo, M. W., &amp; Nerlino, E. (2021).
      Decentralization, teacher quality, and the education of English
      learners: Do state education agencies effectively prepare teachers
      of ELs? <em>Education Policy Analysis Archives, 29</em>(100).
      <ExternalLink class="text-accent hover:underline" href="https://doi.org/10.14507/epaa.29.5279">https://doi.org/10.14507/epaa.29.5279</ExternalLink>
    </p>

    <h2 id={ANCHORS.howToCite} class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">How to cite / attribution</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">
      Use of data, figures, or findings from this catalog in research,
      reporting, policy work, presentations, or other publications
      requires citation of <strong>both</strong> the underlying source
      paper and this site. The paper is the original scholarly work
      that seeded the catalog; citing only the site would obscure the
      authors whose research established the dataset.
    </p>
    <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-semibold text-ink">Source paper (required)</h3>
    <p class="mt-1 text-ink-muted">
      Leider, C. M., Colombo, M. W., &amp; Nerlino, E. (2021).
      Decentralization, teacher quality, and the education of English
      learners: Do state education agencies effectively prepare teachers
      of ELs? <em>Education Policy Analysis Archives, 29</em>(100).
      <ExternalLink class="text-accent hover:underline" href="https://doi.org/10.14507/epaa.29.5279">https://doi.org/10.14507/epaa.29.5279</ExternalLink>
    </p>
    <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-semibold text-ink">This site</h3>
    <p class="mt-1 text-ink-muted">
      projectcert. <em>An atlas of U.S. state teacher certification
      requirements for instructing classified English Learner students.</em>
      Retrieved {new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10)} from
      <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href={ROUTES.home}>this website</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-muted">
      Each state page also lists the underlying SEA documents that
      ground every fact, alongside their retrieval dates. Quotations
      of specific requirements should cite the SEA source directly in
      addition to the entries above.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Contributing</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">
      The state records are maintained in a public project repository.
      Proposed updates — new SEA documents, changed credentialing
      requirements, corrections — should be submitted as an issue or
      pull request with the source URL and retrieval date.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
